<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 104,064 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 104,064 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 104,064 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 98,809 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   April 1</p>
<p>    Export cargo		19,377	15,934</p>
<p>    Import cargo		84,687	82,875</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight are expected to sail and seven are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		68,000	 Johar		  4/4</p>
<p>Mogas		    25,000	 San Sebastian	4/4</p>
<p>Iron scrap	     10,106	 J. Profits	   7/4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
